  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "The operator MLD is meant to use the density criterion that defines mlotst, so the exact sigma-t/buoyancy threshold, local-pressure evaluation and online-then-monthly-averaged construction of mlotst constrain the offline computation and explain possible disagreement.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`mlotst` is referenced to the ocean surface, so pass `ref_depth` = the model's shallowest level to `compute_mixed_layer_depth` (default 10 m is wrong here); compute the MLD of each monthly profile, never MLD of time-averaged T/S.",
        "State the three residual causes vs `mlotst`: reference level, density form (displaced parcel at local pressure vs σ0 difference), and time averaging (monthly means are averaged profiles, so the operator MLD comes out shallower); exclude columns where the threshold is never reached and report the excluded area — GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR fill them near full column depth, CESM2 often 0 m."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The operator MLD is a nonlinear diagnostic computed offline from monthly thetao and so, so it differs from the model's own mlotst averaged online, and this caveat must be stated when interpreting the consistency test.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f: the operator computes diagnostic-first on monthly profiles, which is not the model's online time-mean MLD; state this order explicitly and do not attribute the residual to model error.",
        "Day weights do not enter a monthly climatology: average each calendar month's 30 values plainly (no `temporal_aggregate` weighting needed)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The bias, RMSD, correlation and ranking must be computed only on a common mask where both fields are defined, matching the question's all-30-instances mask and its cross-model ranking requirement.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put both fields on one grid per model, build one mask over both with `build_comparison_mask` and apply with `.where(mask)` before any bias, RMSE or correlation; report the mask cell counts alongside the metrics.",
        "`ocean_only=True` is only correct when WOA23 is part of the comparison (it is not here) — pass `ocean_only=False`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Building the mask, differences, correlations and coverage percentages requires CF masking of CMIP6 missing values so land and below-sea-floor cells do not contaminate the statistics.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself (`thetao`, `so`, `mlotst` masks can differ); use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same cells, and treat values near 1e20 as unmasked fill, not results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "The offline density criterion must use thetao as potential temperature, which constrains the MLD calculation from the model's temperature field.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature referenced to 0 dbar: use the potential-temperature route in any density calculation (as `temperature_kind()` reads from metadata), not the in-situ route."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "Computing density from CMIP6 so requires treating it as Practical Salinity and deriving Absolute Salinity for TEOS-10 routines, which affects the operator MLD.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is practical salinity with units string `0.001`; do not multiply by 0.001 or 1000 — the numbers are already of order 35 — but convert S_P to S_A before calling gsw routines that expect Absolute Salinity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The area percentages and area-weighted surface statistics must use areacello over the relevant ocean cells rather than simple cell counts.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Area-weight every map statistic with `areacello` (`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`); the exceedance-fraction percentage must be a share of area, not of cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
